    "text": "A vertical pole fixed to the horizontal ground is divided in the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>7</mn></math> by a mark on it with lower part shorter than the upper part. If the two parts subtend equal angles at a point on the ground <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> away from the base of the pole, then the height of the pole (in meters) is :"
